{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he chose a first portion for himself.</b> And he was worthy of this, for truly when Gad chose the land of Sihon and Og, even though it does not have the sanctity of the other side of the Jordan, his intention was to attain something of fundamental importance to him: for there, in the land of Sihon and Og, lay the buried portion of the lawgiver — that portion in which the lawgiver is buried, namely Moses." "<b>And he came at the head of the people.</b> And there, in the land of Sihon and Og, the lawgiver came at the head of the people to conquer the land." "<b>The righteousness of HaShem he performed, and His judgments with Israel.</b> And there the lawgiver performed the righteousness of HaShem for Israel, for there he expounded His Torah. And there he judged with Israel and debated HaShem's ordinances and laws upon them, in the manner of Samuel when he said: הִתְיַצְּבוּ וְאִשָּׁפְטָה אִתְּכֶם אֶת כָּל צִדְקוֹת ה׳ (1 Samuel 12:7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:39.440948751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}